{
  "scope": "Functional layout measured from the reference robot's MJCF at qpos = 0 (straight-leg design pose): joint pivots, joint axes, servo body centres and orientations, and link envelope sizes used as design targets. Numbers only; no surfaces, meshes or CAD are copied. Frame: X forward, Y left, Z up, mm.",
  "source": "https://github.com/pollen-robotics/microduck_rl/tree/2b25a48b08f1f17bc38c90bb03144c81fbd9ed07 (robot_walk.xml + assets), measured with MuJoCo forward kinematics at qpos = 0",
  "why_design_pose": "Measuring at qpos = 0 instead of the HOME pose gives axis-aligned joints, so every bracket is a simple prismatic shape that prints flat. The policy HOME offsets stay in control_interface.json and are applied as joint angles, not baked into the geometry.",
  "servo_class": "XL330 class: body 20 (across) x 34 (long) x 23 (deep), output horn disc 16 dia x 3 with 4 x M2 on a 12 mm circle, matching idler disc on the rear. Case side-hole pattern is NOT modelled; see engineering/actuator_interface.json.",
  "servo_frame": "h = unit vector from the servo body toward its output horn (the child link sits on that side of the pivot); d = unit vector along the body's long axis, with the horn axis 9.5 mm from the short end.",
